## Attribution

The attribution requirement of CC BY 4.0 is satisfied by crediting the
compilation, linking to the licence, and indicating whether changes were made.
Something along these lines is sufficient:

> Contains data derived from **Strike — Singapore Electricity Price Advisory**
> (https://github.com/olenny-coder/sg-electricity-strike-rate), licensed under
> CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Changes were made:
> [describe, or state "no changes"].

A reasonable mechanism is a `NOTICE`, `CREDITS` or `SOURCES` file, or an
attribution line in your own documentation.

